    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "N5SbUd",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 1213,
      "name": "g/stage-engine-off",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "failure",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "A8SKH",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 1236,
      "name": "c/stage-engine-off",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The audio-not-running banner takes the toolbar.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "uuVNz",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 84,
      "name": "t/track-rename",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Track rename",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sUo9u",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 1213,
      "name": "g/track-rename",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "keyboard",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "IwHDm",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 1236,
      "name": "c/track-rename",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The text sheet and keyboard ride over the stage.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "rLceQ",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 84,
      "name": "t/readout",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "7-inch readout",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "YLFCA",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 1213,
      "name": "g/readout",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "second screen",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "S2JTzW",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 1236,
      "name": "c/readout",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The console's other panel: TEMPO and BARS, the beat indicator, the mode chip, and one readoutState word per track.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "WQJ3p",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/signal-loop",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Signal — loop tab",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "RRZ6a",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/signal-loop",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "qRbCe",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/signal-loop",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Monitor-only chip, loaded cards, and the vacant card — bordered like the rest, told apart by “no rack” and the monitor line it omits. Cards sit left-aligned in a wrapping run, fixed 202 wide — the rig decides how many. Until racks exist (#535) row 5 reads “no rack” on every card and the line under it carries the chain run itself; a populated chain switched off reads “Chain off · <run>”; the summary caps at two lines with an ellipsis, which the 196/215 card heights already assume.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "W0tCF",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/signal-input",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Signal — input tab",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "P1n0w",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/signal-input",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "jC7Fd",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/signal-input",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Printed into the take. MODIFIED badge. An input card always carries its monitor line, rack or no rack — whether you hear yourself is a fact about the jack, not about the chain on it. That is where it parts company with the loop face, whose vacant card omits the line because there is no chain to hear. Loopback sockets are excluded from the run — and a rig whose every socket is loopback gets its own empty message (a running engine with nothing capturable), distinct from no sockets at all, which is a stopped engine. MODIFIED compares the live chain against the rack’s saved copy — entry set, order, per-entry bypass, parameter values; a parameter nudged by a MIDI mapping counts, because drift is drift whoever’s finger moved it. The chain’s own power is not part of the comparison: on/off is the card’s switch, not the chain’s content.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "m1bcCE",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/signal-master",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Signal — master tab",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "BKHLZ",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/signal-master",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "zkQJl",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/signal-master",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "One card, summed after this — and the hardware outputs it is summed into, each of which can be switched off. Every one off is the silence the Audio face warns about. Output rows carry the ordinal alone: the engine reports a channel count and no names, so “main” / “phones” on a 20-output interface would label sockets wired to something else. And the master card’s panel has no level and no “in the mix” — the sum has neither a volume nor a mute in the rig.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Xu3Jv",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/signal-detail",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Signal — rack detail",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ZhTwu",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/signal-detail",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "H4NXZs",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/signal-detail",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Rack chooser, the chain as chips, the level and whether it is in the mix at all. A boolean inside a stack of segmented rows stays segmented; a boolean in a list row is a switch — which is why the master face’s per-output booleans are switches and “in the mix” is not. “Hear while playing” is input-only: the tri-state exists for auto, which resolves against the record arm, and only a hardware input can be armed — the row is omitted on loop, track and master. The chain caption carries the chain’s own power (“Chain on” / “Chain off”, the consequence sentence in warning beside it while off — without the pill, a chain switched off by a pedal could never be switched back on) and “Re-sync from input”, offered only while the routed input has an audible chain to copy. An overdub taken against a since-edited input chain shows the mismatch note above the chain: it is captured dry and does not re-inherit.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "T5RJHF",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/fx-edit",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Signal — effect editor",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "T4Y1ej",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/fx-edit",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "editor",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "JgEVB",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/fx-edit",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The same tile grid a plugin gets — a built-in's two parameters are two tiles, not two full-width faders. One design at two zoom levels, so a rig with a Tremolo and a rig with a 24-band compressor read the same way.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sactA",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/fx-reorder",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Chain — drag to reorder",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "jqYla",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/fx-reorder",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "reorder",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "HzJ3S",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/fx-reorder",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Drag a chip; a 4px accent bar on a neighbour’s leading or trailing edge marks where it lands. No slot opens between chips — a finger-wide gap has to come out of the run, which relays the whole strip the instant a press matures: chips sliding, rows appearing and disappearing, and on a scrolled 1024×600 console the panel shortening, the scroll clamping, and the run sliding out from under the finger. Each chip’s two halves are the drop targets instead — a far bigger target than any gap between chips could be. The add chip stays in place during a drag and only goes dark: removing it could empty a row and shorten the panel the same way.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "X6j3Uu",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/fx-plugin",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Signal — plugin editor",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "HKN3B",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/fx-plugin",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "editor",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "CiDK7",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/fx-plugin",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "A hosted VST3. Every parameter is a 78px tile on a 7px gutter, and the kind of parameter picks the tile: continuous and stepped read a value, stepCount 1 is a switch cell, 2–24 is an enum cell, a read-only one is borderless and untappable. Bypass is not a tile — it sits in the chain chrome, once.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Q5S7c",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/library",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Rack library",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "NtcZU",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/library",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Ap1Qr",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/library",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Chains as removable chips, + New rack. The library is global to the rig — racks live beside the device-keyed settings, not inside a session (#442 D1). A session carries references, and a take that inherited a rack carries a frozen copy under the rack’s name: loading a session on another rig must not silently rewrite that rig’s racks, and deleting a rack must not reach into takes that already sound like it. A session bundle embeds the racks it references, so a session moves rigs whole.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Nh09G",
      "x": 16352,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/fx-add",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Add an effect — picker",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "XotMB",
      "x": 16352,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/fx-add",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "j8HZv",
      "x": 16352,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/fx-add",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The seven built-ins, a recent plugin shelf, and Browse all. A plugin chip carries its format as the second line — the machine fact under the name — which is also what keeps the cell at the shared two-line height. A name too long for one line truncates; it never wraps, because the grid’s label is single-line. 746 wide, not 744: four 166px columns need 694, plus 25 padding either side and the 1px border each side. Zero slack — a future padding tweak would silently halve the column count. Mid-scan the count row reads “Looking for plugins…”: a count of zero mid-scan is not a fact about the machine.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "FH1i0",
      "x": 18396,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/fx-browse",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Plugin browser — search",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "bLDv2",
      "x": 18396,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/fx-browse",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "browser",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "NcRRC",
      "x": 18396,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/fx-browse",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Search over 103 installed plugins. Results are a full-bleed grid: the cells stretch to fill the sheet rather than sitting at the fixed chip width, which on a 1880-wide sheet would strand two thirds of it empty. The keyboard’s action key dismisses — there is nothing here to commit, since tapping a result is the commit. The header carries Rescan: a plugin installed after first boot could never appear without it. While a scan runs the control becomes a stop and the sheet shows its progress — a long scan must be interruptible.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "taAEh",
      "x": 20440,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/rack-new",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "New rack — name sheet",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "FI7vb",
      "x": 20440,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/rack-new",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "keyboard",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "vrwMI",
      "x": 20440,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/rack-new",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Unmasked text sheet with Create. Saving names the chain as it stands — entries, order, per-entry bypass, parameters. The name is the only thing asked for, because everything else is already on screen behind the sheet.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "jPesS",
      "x": 22484,
      "y": 1584,
      "name": "t/rack-delete",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Delete rack — confirm",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "z5MMLT",
      "x": 22484,
      "y": 2713,
      "name": "g/rack-delete",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "destructive",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "BTHLZ",
      "x": 22484,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/rack-delete",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Names what is loaded and what deleting costs. Deleting never touches a card that has the rack loaded — the loaded chain is the card’s own copy and keeps playing; it simply reads “no rack” the next time it is drawn. Frozen inherited copies in existing takes keep the dead rack’s name: there, the name is provenance, not a live reference.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "g89Zc",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/control-midi",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Control — MIDI",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Z3Tuhq",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/control-midi",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "vtMt1",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/control-midi",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Device, status line, and the mapping list. Sweeps and switches, global to the rig. “Simulate input” feeds a synthetic event in wherever a real one would land — a listening learn capture first, else the open row, else it is dimmed. The event enters through the controller seam itself, the same shape a real CC delivers, so nothing downstream can tell the difference and nothing grows a test-only branch.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "A6SGV",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-sweep",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — sweep expanded",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lBWwt",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-sweep",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "g23gw6",
      "x": 12264,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-sweep",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "LO and HI calibrate the pedal’s travel. Simulate on the open row runs that row alone: a ramp LO → HI → LO through the row’s own curve, slow enough to watch the target move — the point is seeing the calibration take effect, not proving an event arrives.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hVSUr",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-switch",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — switch expanded",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "T1gWmI",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-switch",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Un5I6",
      "x": 14308,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-switch",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "THRESH plus Toggle / Momentary. Simulate on the open row sends a press-and-release pair through the row’s own threshold and behaviour — a Toggle row flips once, a Momentary row holds and lets go.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "w0KrR",
      "x": 16352,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-stale",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — missing target",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "GYq1r",
      "x": 16352,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-stale",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "failure",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Ya8gK",
      "x": 16352,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-stale",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "What this mapping pointed at no longer exists.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "MB8Ci",
      "x": 18396,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-listening",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — listening",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ZxkVp",
      "x": 18396,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-listening",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "in flight",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "qwASN",
      "x": 18396,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-listening",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Move the control you want to use.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "stICu",
      "x": 20440,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-replace",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — replace prompt",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "S28e8",
      "x": 20440,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-replace",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lFtfO",
      "x": 20440,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-replace",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "That control already drives another mapping.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "jPFet",
      "x": 22484,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-no-device",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — no device",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "I7ZPG",
      "x": 22484,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-no-device",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "off",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hT84d",
      "x": 22484,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-no-device",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The looper runs from the keyboard and mouse.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "NtTse",
      "x": 24528,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-gone",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — device gone",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Xpwnu",
      "x": 24528,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-gone",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "failure",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "CTjXL",
      "x": 24528,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-gone",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "It will reconnect when plugged in.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "NKrKw",
      "x": 26572,
      "y": 3084,
      "name": "t/midi-open-failed",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "MIDI — could not open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "VrvaA",
      "x": 26572,
      "y": 4213,
      "name": "g/midi-open-failed",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "failure",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "E0JH7P",
      "x": 26572,
      "y": 4236,
      "name": "c/midi-open-failed",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "In use by another app.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "e0OTkx",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4584,
      "name": "t/loop",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Loop — tempo",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ubCp0",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 5713,
      "name": "g/loop",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "QPOTZ",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 5736,
      "name": "c/loop",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Tempo, time signature, length, quantise, count-in, sync. Length is a MULTIPLE of the base loop the first take defines (Auto/x1/x2/x3) — the app has no bars figure behind it.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "CoK4X",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 4584,
      "name": "t/loop-tempo",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Tempo — tap or type",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "O0mBo3",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 5713,
      "name": "g/loop-tempo",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "keyboard",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "qCzxO",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 5736,
      "name": "c/loop-tempo",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "A tap pad beside the number pad; the row only says 'tap or type' because both work. Tap goes straight to the engine and the field then MIRRORS what the engine made of it — a tapped tempo is runtime state with nothing to submit. The first keypress replaces the shown tempo rather than appending. Backspace is an icon, not '⌫': the text face has no U+232B and a tofu box is a worse mark than none.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "d1Gx3b",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 4584,
      "name": "t/loop-quantise",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Quantise — picker",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "BuaiV",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 5713,
      "name": "g/loop-quantise",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "SUIKg",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 5736,
      "name": "c/loop-quantise",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The row opens IN PLACE into a chip grid — the app's own six divisions (Off, 1 bar, 1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16), not the four this screen used to draw. Short bare tokens go in a grid, not one 70px row each; annotated options stay rows (see loop-mode-pick).",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Cu7nn",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 4584,
      "name": "t/loop-click",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Loop — click",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "MKo6X",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 5713,
      "name": "g/loop-click",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "l2kYkY",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 5736,
      "name": "c/loop-click",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "When the metronome plays, where it goes, how loud. The bar spans the whole gain stage (0..2, the engine's LE_MAX_GAIN) and reads percent-of-unity, so a normal click sits at half the bar. Output is a bitmask over hardware outputs, summarised: nowhere / all outputs / Out 1 · Out 2 / N outputs.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "M7cWXn",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 4584,
      "name": "t/loop-mode",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Loop — mode",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "xziHG",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 5713,
      "name": "g/loop-mode",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "p4zshY",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 5736,
      "name": "c/loop-mode",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The five LooperMode values, one-shot tracks, and the looper defaults. One-shot is rig-wide and reads OFF on an empty session — `every` on an empty list is vacuously true, which is never what the row means.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "H8MjTh",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 4584,
      "name": "t/settings-mode-confirm",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Mode — clear & switch",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "wI3rr",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 5713,
      "name": "g/settings-mode-confirm",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "destructive",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "wWab0",
      "x": 10220,
      "y": 5736,
      "name": "c/settings-mode-confirm",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Switching mode clears every track, so it confirms first. Identical to loop-mode-pick with the dialog over it — the chooser stays OPEN behind the confirm, and a declined confirm leaves it open, because the user is still choosing.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pH2NU",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 6084,
      "name": "t/tracks",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Tracks — names",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "LyMxV",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7213,
      "name": "g/tracks",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "uDBgi",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7236,
      "name": "c/tracks",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Rename any track; the name is what the stage, the pedal targets and the readout all show. The list follows the rig's own track count — every track, not the showing bank: naming, length and routing are setup, not performance.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "r3tmn",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 6084,
      "name": "t/tracks-lengths",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Tracks — lengths",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "aA65M",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 7213,
      "name": "g/tracks-lengths",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "jAAVw",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 7236,
      "name": "c/tracks-lengths",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Auto takes its length from the first take; a preset records that many bars. The readout is lower case like every other mono readout on this surface — rows 5-8 read 'Auto' before this and were stale copies of the base row. Tapping a row opens TRACKS / tracks-length-pick.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "WLqYg",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 6084,
      "name": "t/tracks-routing",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Tracks — routing",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "YGfo6",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 7213,
      "name": "g/tracks-routing",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "nJgd6",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 7236,
      "name": "c/tracks-routing",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Each track's inputs, outputs and quantize override at a glance. A track with two inputs records two lanes; the inputs read ascending, since this is a summary of the SET and lane order is the panel's business. The footnote wraps at the console's own prose measure rather than running the full width.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "boZ7P",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 6084,
      "name": "t/track-routing",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Track settings dialog",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "xQ9WI",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 7213,
      "name": "g/track-routing",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "lQW4G",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 7236,
      "name": "c/track-routing",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Each checked input is a lane; opening one shows that lane's own outputs, in the drawer the rest of the console opens rows into (LOOP / loop-output's grid, not the older inline block this screen used to draw). Effects stay on the Signal page. BUILT: the panel is capped to the screen and its two groups scroll, since an eight-input rig with a lane open is taller than 1080. The group captions are sticky — the current one pins overhead and is pushed out by the next, and the one you have NOT reached waits at the bottom edge until its own caption rises into view, so both of the panel's questions are visible from the start. The lane's output readout is set in the mono face, like the same string one screen over on tracks-routing.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "N3KVv",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 6084,
      "name": "t/track-unrouted",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Track settings — unrouted",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "P1p7l",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 7213,
      "name": "g/track-unrouted",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "failure",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "RCzKU",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 7236,
      "name": "c/track-unrouted",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "A lane routed nowhere records but is never heard — said on the lane, where the outputs are. The warning is the console's own banner (red dot, 11px, the sentence beside it), inside the lane's drawer rather than over the whole panel: 'this track is silent' is no longer the same statement as 'this lane is'.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Go07e",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7584,
      "name": "t/audio",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Audio — device",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Y3an5f",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 8713,
      "name": "g/audio",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "base",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "TQVrs",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 8736,
      "name": "c/audio",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Device, sample rate and buffer, named inputs, and the round-trip measurement. FOUR rows, not three: the Status tab was dissolved into this one, because everything it reported was either duplicated from here or belonged beside the setting that decides it. The measurement keeps an explicit MEASURE button — merging the readout and the action into a bare tappable row left nothing on screen saying the row did anything. Record offset rides as the latency row's subtitle: it is a consequence of the measurement, not a setting. No round-trip ESTIMATE — two buffer periods cannot include converter latency, so it read as authoritative and was not (#528).",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "bx06I",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 7584,
      "name": "t/settings-device",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Audio — device picker",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "w0mxYi",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 8713,
      "name": "g/settings-device",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "y1pDdi",
      "x": 2044,
      "y": 8736,
      "name": "c/settings-device",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Checked, alternative, unplugged-disabled. Devices stay PICK ROWS while the other lists became chip grids — a device carries its channel counts and a long name, so it is not a bare token.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "VMrNc",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 7584,
      "name": "t/settings-rate",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Audio — rate and buffer",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "A6qiis",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 8713,
      "name": "g/settings-rate",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "N38SX6",
      "x": 4088,
      "y": 8736,
      "name": "c/settings-rate",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Sample rate and buffer as CHIP GRIDS, not row lists. Dropping the per-option latency left bare tokens, and a bare token has nothing to put in a row's width — a column of 70px rows spent 1,600px on four characters.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ljNNo",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 7584,
      "name": "t/settings-inputs",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Audio — inputs",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "j49iXu",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 8713,
      "name": "g/settings-inputs",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "open",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Xk57L",
      "x": 6132,
      "y": 8736,
      "name": "c/settings-inputs",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The hardware says input 2; you say mic. Each chip is a COLUMN — the name on top, `input 2` under it in grey — so the socket is always legible and the name is only what you call it. An unnamed chip is the bare `input 3`, centred, in the primary ink (see settings-inputs-unnamed for why the tone moves). Tapping a chip renames it; see settings-inputs-wide for an 18-in rig (#528).",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "wo0VZ",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 7584,
      "name": "t/settings-rename",
      "fill": "#ffffff",
      "content": "Audio — rename input",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "JKR7o",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 8713,
      "name": "g/settings-rename",
      "fill": "#738cf2",
      "content": "keyboard",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontWeight": "600"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ppxui",
      "x": 8176,
      "y": 8736,
      "name": "c/settings-rename",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The input list plus the rename sheet and keyboard.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
    {
