              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HGvzH",
                  "name": "B",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Tile grid is the overview; tapping a tile opens the full-width row as an editor sheet. A and B are the same design at two zoom levels, not two designs.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "S49PAM",
                  "name": "B",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "C and D both lose on the one axis that made us drop the knob. A 44px fader or a 76px bar is no more precise than a 36px rotary — swapping an imprecise round control for an imprecise flat one fixes the grip problem and keeps the accuracy problem.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "uXCEB",
                  "name": "B",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The extra tap is affordable here specifically. This is a looper with a foot pedal: live, mid-take control belongs to the pedal, so the screen's job is setup and overview rather than performance. That is what makes A's cost cheap and C/D's precision loss expensive.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "H63wn",
                  "name": "B",
                  "fill": "$text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "It reuses a pattern the console already has — tempo is edited exactly this way today, via a value that opens a keypad sheet.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": "$text-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
