    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "V44Nxq",
      "x": 30484,
      "y": 8736,
      "name": "c/settings-inputs-unnamed",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "The first-run state, and the reason the ordinal changes tone: an unnamed chip carries `input 3` in the PRIMARY ink because it is the only thing the chip says, while a named one drops it to grey under the name. Held at grey throughout, a rig where nothing is named would be a grid of entirely grey chips — which reads as disabled rather than as nothing having been said about them yet. The row above reads `none named` (#528).",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
