    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "Cd6s8",
      "x": 26572,
      "y": 2736,
      "name": "c/master-last-output",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "Out 1 is already off; the tap on Out 2 stops here instead of landing. Switching the last live output off is the silence the Audio face warns about, and this must not be a way to reach it without being told — so the last one asks, in the warning’s own amber, not the destructive red: nothing is destroyed, and Keep it on costs nothing. The switch itself has not moved yet — the dialog intercepts the write, it does not undo it. Any other output’s switch flips silently, because every other off is reversible by ear.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
