    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "DK4HE",
      "x": 16352,
      "y": 1236,
      "name": "c/device-lost",
      "fill": "#9ea3b0",
      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
      "width": 1800,
      "content": "A toast is for an event; these are conditions, and a condition holds the screen until it stops being true. Device-lost in the record red — the engine is stopped, which is the loudest fact the console has; MIDI-lost in the warning amber, because the loops keep playing without it. Each banner carries the one action that ends it (Choose device / Control), leaves on its own the moment the hardware returns, and stacks in severity order when both hold. The 7-inch readout echoes the same line in its status strip — the performer is looking down, not at this screen. Neither ever appears as a dialog: a lost interface mid-song must not also steal the transport.",
      "fontFamily": "Inter",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontWeight": "normal"
    },
